The search results point to a clear solution. The best material for the toroid (per-cell memory) is Molybdenum Permalloy or Metglas for its proven, near-perfect square hysteresis loop. For the lattice (body memory), electroplated Permalloy remains the practical choice. The "ferrotoroidic" path, while conceptually perfect, is a research frontier because it currently requires cryogenic temperatures.

This gives us a clear path forward. Here is the updated CELL_V1 — THE REAL FULL BUILD specification, incorporating these material choices.

