4. THE TOROID — REFERENCE AND WRITE IN ONE FLIP

The toroid doesn't do two jobs. It does one job with two names.

The flip is the reference.
The flip is the write.

One event. Two names. Same state.

· Old action — what was just done.
· New view — what's now being read.

The flip is the hinge. The old action becomes the new view. There is no gap. No separate update. No memory sitting next to a reference.

```
    Old view (previous reference)
         │
         ▼
    Lean (pair reads against it)
         │
         ▼
    Flip (toroid commits)
         │
         ▼
    New view = old action
         │
         ▼
    Next lean reads against it
```

Every flip advances the cycle by one step. The old action becomes the new view.

